id: pm-rust-long-intent-cursor
title: Verify long producer cursors survive bounded intent compaction
description: "Review thread PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs62QgiY on PR #165 reports that intent compaction may shorten a producer next_cursor beyond 240 UTF-16 units and make --after unusable. Separate from round-four atomic lifecycle admission: reproduce against the pinned oracle in a non-git fixture, preserve cursor validity through the delivery path, and add a behavioral revert test without weakening budget assertions."
type: Task
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: conformance,follow-up,"gh:unbraind/pm-rust#165"
created_at: "2026-11-11T17:58:30.355Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-12T14:25:44.933Z"
author: codex-rust164-1111
parent: pm-rust-oracle-1111
comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-12T01:29:34.962Z",codex-agent,"Round 5 independently reproduced the long producer-cursor defect in the pinned published CLI. A bounded triage page truncates its base64 cursor with an ellipsis. Native recursive compaction now preserves producer/output cursor fields, with a real long-ID fixture proving the emitted native cursor resumes to a different page. This is an intentional continuation-safety divergence under the final-round instruction to repair every valid review finding; no existing differential assertion is changed. Keep the item in progress for orchestrator verification, never close it here."
  "2026-11-12T03:45:22.042Z",codex-agent,The full pagination target passes 30/30 with the required pinned oracle. Native long-ID continuation is executed successfully; the separate oracle observation retains the clipped cursor defect as evidence. The preservation rule protects both producer and output-snapshot cursors without weakening existing byte comparisons. Final-source reruns and the dedicated behavioral negative control are retained on the main oracle item.
  "2026-11-12T05:41:58.013Z",codex-agent,"Round-five final result: full pagination differential passes 30/30. round5_long_intent_cursor_remains_executable independently replays the native continuation with long persisted IDs; the pinned oracle emits a clipped unusable cursor. Reverting compact_strings cursor protection fails at an assertion and restoration passes. Output-snapshot cursors are also protected, validation precedes omission, and the frozen final TOON boundary omits at 3236 tokens and delivers at 3237. Recorded with the code and full evidence in docs/ORACLE_REVIEW_ROUND5_2026_11_12.md. Item remains in progress; releasing only this agent claim."
  "2026-11-12T13:45:26.353Z",codex-agent,"Round seven keeps all native cursor assertions when the published driver is absent, checks the exact frozen eight-row suffix over every continuation, and independently checks invalid native cursors. Only published assertions depend on the oracle. Envelope cursor fields remain intact while equally named nested item metadata is compacted; full-item oracle budget bytes are compared unchanged."
  "2026-11-12T14:25:42.476Z",codex-agent,"Final evidence: full pagination differential target 32/32; explicit missing-oracle invocation of round5_long_intent_cursor_remains_executable passes every native assertion. Reverting compact_strings fails the nested cursor metadata regression; removing only the oracle guard fails the no-oracle regression; injecting an empty continuation fails the exact-suffix regression. Each passes after restoration. Full shared-code differential coverage is 150/150 across eight targets. Work is ready for orchestrator verification; item remains in progress and is not closed."
